To build Lumen from git you need:

-A C compiler (GCC or Clang)
-Meson 0.62+ and Ninja
-Pkg-Config
-GNU Gettext
-Xlib, Xext, Xrandr, Xinerama, Xau library/headers (devel packages)
-Glib 2.28+, libxml2 2.6+, Pango 1.18+ and cairo library/headers (devel packages)

Also you will probably want:
-Imlib2 and librsvg library/headers (devel packages), for icons
-X Cursor library/headers (devel package)
-SM and ICE library/headers (devel packages), for session management
-Startup Notification library/headers 0.8+ (devel package)

Meson enables each of these when it finds it; `meson configure build` lists
the options to turn them off.

Do the following to build and install Lumen from git:

% meson setup build --prefix=/usr --sysconfdir=/etc
% meson compile -C build
% sudo meson install -C build

Don't try running it from the build directory without installing, it won't
work. It needs to be installed before it is run.

The following commands will be available: lumen-wm (and openbox, a link to
  it), openbox-session, openbox-gnome-session and openbox-kde-session.

See the man pages for details about them.  If you want to run Lumen on its
  own, you probably want to run "openbox-session".

----
In Ubuntu, you want these packages:

gcc
gettext
meson
ninja-build
pkg-config
libglib2.0-dev
libxml2-dev
libpango1.0-dev
libcairo2-dev
libx11-dev
libxext-dev
libxrandr-dev
libxinerama-dev
libxau-dev
libxcursor-dev
libsm-dev
libimlib2-dev
librsvg2-dev
libstartup-notification0-dev
